@startuml
title Delivery mode decides whether an unusable recipient is fatal
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}

component "recipient address" as Addr
component "is_valid()\ny² = x³ − 17 solvable at x?" as Valid
component "tagging secret oracle\n(shared secret derived)" as Oracle
component "random secret\nundiscoverable tag" as Rand
component "panic:\nCannot resolve a constrained\ntagging secret" as Panic

Addr --> Valid
Valid --> Oracle : valid
Valid --> Rand : invalid,\nunconstrained / offchain
Valid --> Panic : invalid,\nonchain_constrained

note bottom of Rand
  Best effort: the send succeeds and
  the recipient receives nothing it
  can find. A wrong address stays
  invisible here.
end note

note bottom of Panic
  A proved encryption cannot be served
  for an address with no curve point,
  and must not claim the guarantee
  while emitting an unfindable tag.
end note

note bottom of Valid
  About half of all field elements are
  not x-coordinates of a Grumpkin point.
  Zero is one of them, and zero is the
  default of an unset delayed address.
end note
@enduml
